title: mfr_path
tags: [[Reserved field]] [[File tracking]]
kind: reference
summary: A file's position in the filesystem's tree — a tree_ref, nothing once the file was seen removed.

The field that makes a metarecord a file's. Its value is a `tree_ref` (the parent
directory's metarecord and the name), so the paths form a forest
([[TreeRef path conventions]]). It has four states — a position, a stale position,
`nothing`, no field — listed in [[Reserved fields]]. Only the watcher, `mf orphan clear`
and a forced write set it to `nothing`; reconcile never does ([[Orphans]],
[[Event semantics]]).
